# Exported GitHub threads — someone else's text, written out verbatim by
# `scripts/export-github-item.py`. Reformatting it edits the record, and the
# next export puts it back.
docs/issue
docs/pr

# Generated content renders — produced by `pnpm content:mermaid`, keyed by a
# hash of their source, so reformatting them would only churn the diff.
apps/*/public/generated

# Session cost rows — rewritten wholesale by `.claude/costs/session_cost.py` on
# every turn, so a formatting pass over them is undone by the next one.
.claude/costs/sessions

# Per-machine Claude Code settings — never committed, written by the harness
# rather than by hand, so its formatting is nobody's to hold to a standard.
.claude/settings.local.json

# GitHub exports — `scripts/export-github-item.py` writes what the thread holds,
# and a snapshot reformatted is no longer the thing it is a snapshot of.
docs/issue
docs/pr

